    {
      "title": "8 BJP and 2 SP candidates from UP elected unopposed to Rajya Sabha",
      "link": "https://www.business-standard.com/politics/8-bjp-and-2-sp-candidates-from-up-elected-unopposed-to-rajya-sabha-126100901442_1.html",
      "description": "All 10 Rajya Sabha candidates from Uttar Pradesh -- eight from the Bharatiya Janata Party and two from the Samajwadi Party -- were declared elected unopposed on Friday, an official said.\n\"Except Samajwadi Party candidate Dhanraj Parimal Nathwani, the rest of the winning candidates collected their certificates themselves, though SP leader Ram Gopal Yadav and BJP's Radhakant Ojha got them collected through their representatives,\" Returning Officer for the Rajya Sabha polls Ajit Verma, who is also the Special Secretary of UP Vidhan Sabha, told PTI.\nCongratulating the BJP candidates, Uttar Pradesh Chief Minister Yogi Adityanath, on X in Hindi, said, \"Heartiest congratulations to all BJP candidates from Uttar Pradesh for being elected unopposed in the Rajya Sabha biennial elections-2026.\"\n\"I have full confidence that you all will make a significant contribution in realising the resolve of our Prime Minister @narendramodi ji for 'Viksit Bharat' and in giving new momentum to the nation's .",
      "source_name": "Business Standard Latest",
      "published": "2026-10-09T18:14:11"
    }
